title: Fear of Man or Fear of God: Zedekiah and Jeremiah
description: Posts from the channel on Jeremiah 38: believers who speak boldly though mocked, King Zedekiah's fear of man, and why we set our minds on Christ rather than wait on a leader to save us.
output: lessons/posts/pulled-fear-of-man-zedekiah.html

# From the two posts of 2023-09-30 (studies/data/notes/pulled-fear-of-man-zedekiah.html), in the author's words.

=== Introduction
--- Fear of Man or Fear of God [title]
overline: From the channel
heading: Fear of Man or Fear of God
sub: Zedekiah and Jeremiah
refs: Jeremiah 38:19; Jeremiah 38:20; Matthew 10:28; 2 Peter 3:3-4
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move through the slides. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

=== Jeremiah 38
--- I am afraid of the Jews
scripture: Jeremiah 38:17-20 | mark: I am afraid of the Jews; Obey, I beseech thee, the voice of the LORD
p: This story has so many applications.

--- Tell this Christian to shut up
lead: In the lives of saved believers, we often are mocked and ridiculed for preaching the word of God and telling those in sin that they're wrong.
p: And when these unsaved come to the supposed leaders of churches and denominations, and say "tell this Christian to shut up," essentially, they comply.

--- We have to be loving
p: They say that we have to be loving.
- We can't preach against sin. Against the wicked. Against sodomites and Jews.
- That we can't tell people the judgment of God against those who sin and those who are haters of God.
- That we may offend them.
p: They will even say things like Billy Graham or various Popes; "Jews, Muslims and Hindus who are sincere will find Heaven," knowing the Bible says the only path to the Father is through the Son. [[John 14:6]]

=== For fear of the Jews
--- So much of it comes from fear
lead: And so much of it comes from fear of the Jews.
p: How much dispensationalism and Zionism is preached by pastors who know better, for fear of the Jews?
- Fear of lost funding.
- Fear of being called names by the ADL?
- Fear of being persecuted?
note: [[John 7:13]] [[John 19:38]] [[John 20:19]]

--- Even in our own lives
p: Even in our own lives, we may have relatives or people in our church who tell us to cool it with the antisemitism. Stop speaking out against abominations. To rein in our hatred of every false way. [[Psalm 119:104]]
p: These same types will also wet-blanket soul winning and evangelizing the Gospel. They may even call giving the Gospel to Jews a hate crime.
callout: For fear of the Jews.

=== Speak boldly
--- So we speak boldly
lead: But we know that by following the word of God and fearing only Him, we will be delivered. Even in death, we are delivered.
p: So we speak boldly. We give the Gospel to every creature. We stand against evil and we defend that which is good. Even if it means we are mocked. Because we know the mockers will get their reward. [[Mark 16:15]]

--- The mockers
scripture: 2 Peter 3:3-4 | mark: there shall come in the last days scoffers
p: We know the Lord is not slack concerning his promise. We know the mockers will be destroyed. That we shall overcome and be delivered by our Lord Jesus Christ. [[2 Peter 3:9]]

=== Zedekiah
--- Fear of the Lord and fear of man
lead: King Zedekiah's fear and double-mindedness, and his equivocating between fear of the Lord and fear of man, honestly reminds me so much of supposed leaders like Donald Trump.
p: Trump isn't the only coward like King Zedekiah. All our politicians are craven. All fear the Jews more than the Lord. All fear what men can do to the flesh rather than He who can destroy the soul.
big: Matthew 10:28

--- No help from Egypt
lead: It is why we shouldn't be caught up in waiting for a leader to come to save us.
p: Like the people of Jerusalem who thought the Pharaoh's armies from Egypt would save them from the Chaldeans, but the respite was short lived. And Jerusalem fell anyway. [[Jeremiah 37:7]]

--- Set our minds on Christ [title]
heading: Set our minds on Christ
p: We need to set our minds on Christ. Be led of God through the Spirit. Hearkening to the word of God.
refs: Romans 8:14; Colossians 3:2
